.Dd July 27, 2026
.Dt SECURESPF 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm securespf
.Nd SPF verification milter for Postfix
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl c Ar config-file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a high-performance Sender Policy Framework (SPF) verification milter
implementing RFC 7208.
It integrates with Postfix via the Sendmail milter protocol version 6,
evaluates SPF records for incoming mail, and adds
.Dq Authentication-Results
headers with the SPF verdict.
.Pp
.Nm
uses a thread-per-core architecture with kqueue I/O multiplexing.
Each worker thread owns its own kqueue, connection pool, DNS resolver
with TTL-based caching, and ZMQ publisher socket.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl c Ar config-file
Path to the INI-style configuration file.
Required.
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
The configuration file uses INI format with a
.Ql [global]
section and one or more
.Ql [listener:name]
sections.
.Ss Global Section
.Bl -tag -width "SyslogFacility" -compact
.It Cm AuthservID
Identifier for Authentication-Results headers.
Default:
.Dq localhost .
.It Cm StripAuthResults
Remove every pre-existing Authentication-Results header claiming our
.Cm AuthservID ,
not just the ones asserting an
.Li spf=
result.
Enable this on the first milter in the chain, which sits at the trust boundary
(RFC 8601 Section 5).
Leave it disabled on later milters, which must be able to read the results
earlier ones produced.
Default: no.
.It Cm WorkerThreads
Number of worker threads.
0 means auto-detect CPU count.
Default: 0.
.It Cm MaxConnections
Maximum simultaneous connections per worker.
Default: 256.
.It Cm PidFile
Path to the PID file.
Default:
.Pa /var/run/securespf/securespf.pid .
.It Cm Foreground
Run in foreground without daemonizing.
Default: no.
.It Cm User
Drop privileges to this user after binding sockets.
.It Cm Syslog
Enable syslog output.
Default: yes.
.It Cm SyslogFacility
Syslog facility.
One of: mail, daemon, local0\(enlocal7.
Default: mail.
.It Cm LogLevel
Logging verbosity.
One of: err, warn, info, debug.
Default: info.
.It Cm DnsNameserver
Comma-separated list of DNS nameserver IP addresses.
Default:
.Dq 127.0.0.1 .
.It Cm DnsTimeout
DNS query timeout in seconds.
Default: 5.
.It Cm DnsRetries
Number of DNS query retries.
Default: 2.
.It Cm DnsCacheSize
Maximum entries in the per-worker DNS cache.
Default: 1000.
.It Cm DnsNegativeTTL
TTL in seconds for negative DNS cache entries (NXDOMAIN, SERVFAIL).
Default: 60.
.It Cm WhitelistFile
Path to a file containing IP addresses (one per line) that bypass SPF checks.
.It Cm MaxHeaders
Largest number of headers accumulated for one message.
Default: 500.
0 disables the limit.
.It Cm MaxHeaderBytes
Largest total header size, names plus values, accumulated for one message.
Accepts an optional
.Cm K , Cm M
or
.Cm G
suffix.
Default: 1M.
0 disables the limit.
.Pp
SPF is evaluated from the envelope sender and client address, so
.Nm
never buffers a message body and has no
.Cm MaxBodyBytes .
It does accumulate the header block, in order to strip
.Cm Authentication-Results
headers forging its own
.Cm AuthservID .
.Pp
A message exceeding either limit is tempfailed rather than delivered.
Headers past the limit are never read, and
.Nm
can only strip a forged header that it read, so delivering the message would let
one hidden beyond the limit through uninspected.
Raise these if legitimate mail crossing many forwarders and mailing lists is
being deferred.
Both are read at startup only;
.Dv SIGHUP
does not change them.
.It Cm MaxVoidLookups
Largest number of terms in one SPF record whose DNS lookup finds nothing \(en
either an authoritative
.Dq no such name
or an empty answer.
Default: 2.
0 disables the limit.
.Pp
RFC 7208 \(sc4.6.4 makes this limit a
.Em SHOULD
and recommends 2, which is why it is configurable while the other processing
limits are not.
Exceeding it produces
.Cm permerror .
.It Cm MaxEvaluationMs
Wall-clock ceiling, in milliseconds, on evaluating one message.
Default: 20000.
0 disables the limit.
.Pp
RFC 7208 \(sc4.6.4 requires a time limit without naming a value; the 20 seconds
suggested in \(sc10.1 for a complete check is the closest thing to a specified
one.
Exhausting the budget produces
.Cm temperror ,
not a verdict: the evaluation was incomplete, and answering
.Cm fail
would reject mail on the strength of terms that were never read.
.Pp
Two further limits from \(sc4.6.4 are fixed at 10 and deliberately not
configurable, because senders design their records against those exact numbers:
the count of DNS-querying terms per evaluation
.Pq Cm a , Cm mx , Cm ptr , Cm exists , Cm include No and Cm redirect ,
and the count of records examined inside a single
.Cm mx
or
.Cm ptr
mechanism.
.Pp
When either of these limits or any other condition ends an evaluation early,
.Nm
logs a second line for the message carrying
.Cm reason=
and the RFC section, because
.Cm permerror
alone does not distinguish a limit from a malformed record.
.It Cm ZmqEndpoint
ZeroMQ PUB endpoint for event publishing (e.g.,
.Dq tcp://events.internal:5555 ) .
Disabled if not set.
.It Cm ZmqTopic
ZeroMQ topic prefix.
Default:
.Dq spf.result .
.El
.Ss Listener Sections
Each
.Ql [listener:name]
section defines a socket to listen on.
.Bl -tag -width "Socket" -compact
.It Cm Socket
Listen address.
Format:
.Dq inet:port@host
for TCP or
.Dq unix:/path/to/socket
for Unix domain sockets.
.El
.Pp
If no listener sections are defined, the default is
.Dq inet:8890@0.0.0.0 .
.Sh SIGNALS
.Bl -tag -width "SIGTERM" -compact
.It Dv SIGHUP
Reload configuration file.
Active connections are not interrupted.
.It Dv SIGTERM
Graceful shutdown.
Stops accepting new connections and drains active ones (30 second timeout).
.El
.Sh POSTFIX INTEGRATION
Add to
.Pa main.cf :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
smtpd_milters = inet:127.0.0.1:8890
milter_connect_macros = j {daemon_name} v {client_addr}
milter_default_action = accept
.Ed
.Pp
The
.Cm {client_addr}
macro is required for
.Nm
to see the SMTP client's IP address.
.Sh LOG FORMAT
Each processed message produces one info-level syslog line:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
securespf[pid]: id=QUEUEID peer=HOST[IP] client=IP from=ADDR result=VERDICT elapsed=Nms
.Ed
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/local/etc/securespf/securespf.conf"
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/securespf/securespf.conf
Default configuration file location.
.It Pa /var/run/securespf/securespf.pid
Default PID file location.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr securedkim 8 ,
.Xr securedmarc 8 ,
.Xr securearc 8 ,
.Xr securespf-check 8 ,
.Xr postconf 5
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%T Sender Policy Framework (SPF) for Authorizing Use of Domains in Email
.%R RFC 7208
.Re
